# Build & Install Workflow

## Default behaviour after code changes

**Build for compilation check only** — do not install on device unless the user
explicitly asks to test on the phone.

```
# ✅ Default — compile check only
Set-Location "c:\projects\healthings-medilab\app\android"
.\gradlew.bat assembleRelease --no-build-cache

# ✅ Only when user says "install" / "test on phone" / "let me test"
adb install -r "...\app-release.apk"
```

## When to install
- User explicitly says: "install", "test on phone", "let me try it", "rebuild and install"
- After a bug fix the user reported from a device screenshot
- At the end of a feature batch when the user asks to verify

## When NOT to install automatically
- After every small fix (wastes 30–40 seconds per iteration)
- After a compilation-only change (import cleanup, type fix, dead code removal)
- When the user just asked to "rebuild" without mentioning the phone

## Commit policy — NEVER commit before phone test

**Do NOT `git commit` or `git push` after a feature build until the user explicitly
confirms they tested the APK on their phone and it works.**

Trigger words that mean "ok to commit":
- "commit", "push", "lgtm", "looks good", "works", "it's working", "ship it"

Trigger words that mean "NOT ok to commit yet":
- "build", "compile check", "let me test", "install" — wait for test result first

```
# ✅ Correct order
1. Build APK  →  2. Install on phone (when asked)  →  3. User tests  →  4. User says "commit"  →  5. git commit & push

# ❌ Never do
Build APK  →  git commit  (skips phone test)
```

## Build command (PowerShell — no && separator)

**Show live progress** when the user is waiting (build / install). Do **not** pipe to
`Select-Object -Last N` — that hides output until the end and looks frozen.

```powershell
$env:GRADLE_USER_HOME = "C:\gradle-hm"   # short path — avoids Windows 260-char CMake failures
Set-Location "c:\projects\healthings-medilab\app\android"
.\gradlew.bat assembleRelease --no-build-cache --console=plain
```

Agent-only quick tail (user not watching): last 12 lines is OK.

## Clean build (only when native modules / codegen errors)
```powershell
$env:GRADLE_USER_HOME = "C:\gradle-hm"
Set-Location "c:\projects\healthings-medilab\app\android"
.\gradlew.bat assembleRelease --no-build-cache --console=plain
```
